56.286Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/006-epic-review.json","content":"{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Two independent reviewers produced conflicting outcomes (pass vs block). The reverifier's task is to determine whether the blocking findings (EV-001, EV-002) are substantiated by the codebase and epic artifacts, and whether the non-blocking design risks cited by Reviewer 1 (NF-002, NF-004) properly account for the issues raised by Reviewer 2. Per conservative reverify protocol, blockers are downgraded only when explicit evidence disproves them. The reverification examined the disputed surfaces: (1) Story 3's corpus verification path against AC-6.1's recorded PI corpora requirement; (2) Story 1's reload semantics against AC-1.5's exact-thread reconstruction requirement. Findings follow.\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 2-5 are coherent across the capture/fork/inference/startup-validation spine: all paths route through connector entry points and real LHC intake/scheduler/inspect surfaces (both reviewers agree).\",\"Story 1 has a lifecycle coverage gap: reload for no-flag and --resume launches reattaches by cwd-most-recent registry row, not by durable resolved-threadId reconstruction (Reviewer 2 block EV-002; Reviewer 1 NF-002 as accepted constraint).\",\"Story 3 does not satisfy the epic-level verification contract: corpus fixtures are simplified AgentMessage JSONL rows paired with handcrafted expected events, not recorded PI hook/lifecycle corpora as required by AC-6.1 (Reviewer 2 block EV-001; Reviewer 1 claims real corpora used).\",\"Plain-data-only rule is enforced across all lifecycle paths—SessionState contains only ThreadRef + flags, no PI objects retained (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Capture flow is consistent: index.ts orchestrates map → accumulate → batch flush through converter for all message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select hooks (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Fork detection and seeding logic properly wired in session_start handler with both hook-based and session-tree fallback evidence paths (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Startup validation correctly runs after instance creation but before capture begins, leaving capture running on validation failure per AC-5.3 (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"The --resume picker has an interactive ctx.ui.select path for multi-candidate scenarios, while headless multi-candidate resume remains fail-closed requiring explicit --session (Reviewer 2; not disputed).\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Module boundaries respected: check-boundaries.mjs passes (20 src files checked) (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Interfaces match tech design Interface Definitions—all required exports present with correct signatures (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Hook rail matches EPIC_1_HOOKS specification—all observe-only hooks registered, context hook correctly omitted (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Converter architecture matches tech design: map-message is pure, TurnAccumulator owns the LHC turn boundary, converter flushes through intakeStream.messageEvents (both reviewers agree).\",\"Local PI types in src/pi/types.ts mirror verified v0.79.2 contract since @earendil-works/* packages aren't build dependencies yet (Reviewer 1 NF-004; Reviewer 2 NF-002).\",\"initLhc is thin wrapper over createSdk per tech-arch A-4—mechanical rename pending LHC package change (Reviewer 1 NF-005).\",\"The observe-only boundary is preserved: index.ts registers no context hook, capture does not alter PI's model context path (Reviewer 2; not disputed).\",\"Derived-form reuse is deferred while fork correctness is preserved—fork requeues derived forms on new thread rather than copying/reusing per tech design I-2 (Reviewer 1 NF-003; Reviewer 2 NF-003).\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 33 TCs mapped to tests—test-plan.md TC→Test mapping fully realized (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Architecture-risk tests present: 7 tests covering restart survival, idempotency double-replay, failure classification, capture isolation, fork source immutability, fixture validity, concurrency (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Foundation tests present: 7 tests covering corpus shapes, synthetic builders, temp-thread factory, extension-load smoke, verification-config (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Total test coverage: 144 tests passing across 20 test files (Reviewer 1; Reviewer 2 gates also passed).\",\"Flows 2-5 are covered by source and tests: ordered capture, turn derivation, idempotency, fork replay, model-call routing, classified failures, startup validation (Reviewer 2).\",\"Flow 1 is partially covered: launch creation, named resolution, continue, interactive resume, shutdown implemented; exact same-thread reload not implemented for no-flag and --resume launches (Reviewer 2).\",\"Flow 6 is incomplete against AC-6.1: replay is deterministic and compares events/messages/turns, but does not consume recorded PI corpora as required (Reviewer 2 EV-001).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Production createModelCall uses real PI modelRegistry.find and hasConfiguredAuth—no fake adapters in production inference path (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Extension entry point (index.ts activate) registers real hooks with production defaults (~/.lhc registry, process.argv launch flags, real ModelCall) (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"No shims or placeholders in production capture path—converter, idempotency, turn-accumulator all use real implementations (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Startup validation uses real PI modelRegistry for reachability probes—correctly classifies unknown_model vs auth_not_configured (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\"Test-only model-call fakes a